  "id": "attribution-theory",
  "term": "attribution theory",
  "definition": "Attribution theory is a way of explaining people’s reactions by considering what causes they assign to an event or experience. In this source, it is used as a three-dimensional framework that groups causes into individual, informational, and situational factors and emphasizes that their combined influence shapes outcomes such as health information anxiety.",
